Game Stream for Ubuntu amd64
===========================

Install with:
  sudo apt install ./game-stream_0.2.4_amd64.deb

Open Applications > Game Stream. First launch requires internet and about 2 GB
of free disk space for its private Python dependencies and Chromium browser.
A progress dialog reports setup. Native system dependencies are installed by
apt; no Python packages or browsers are downloaded by root maintainer scripts.
The per-user runtime is under ~/.local/share/game-stream (or XDG_DATA_HOME).
If interrupted, launch again. A previous working runtime is kept if an update
fails. Setup diagnostics are in ~/.local/state/game-stream/setup.log.

Close the app before uninstalling. Run as the normal desktop user:
  game-stream-uninstall
Optional removal of this user's preferences/session/catalog:
  game-stream-uninstall --purge-user-data
Dry run:
  game-stream-uninstall --dry-run

Or remove only the system package:
  sudo apt remove game-stream
This preserves user runtime/settings; the uninstall helper removes the owned
runtime too. Never run the application itself with sudo.

Ubuntu 22.04/24.04/26.04 amd64 with Python 3.10-3.15 is the intended target.
Other desktop Linux distributions can use the documented source installation.
This is not an Android APK and does not run on Android.

Standalone uninstall tools are also distributed with each release:
  bash uninstall-game-stream.sh [--dry-run] [--purge-user-data]
The game-stream-uninstaller_0.2.4.tar.gz bundle contains this script and instructions.

Release 0.2.4 adds Alt+1-4 pane counts, Shift+1-3 large-stream selection,
G layout toggle, H shortcut reference, Default/Light/Dark themes,
overlay opacity (25-100%, default 85%) and button text size (9-24px, default 12px).
Controls wrap inside narrow panes when needed. Preferences has Playback,
Appearance and Updates tabs; Show browser, Solo audio and Check/Install Updates
are located there. Cookie buttons and the App menu are removed.
Update checks save settings and close the modal before starting the updater.
Updates verify a .deb from the project's GitHub repository, save/close the app,
request administrator authorization with pkexec, install and reopen as the user.
For this private repository, use 'gh auth login' with an account that can read it.
Diagnostics are in ~/.local/state/game-stream/update.log. Each recipient of
private updates needs repository access. Download failures leave playback running.

Browser source quality defaults to 720p when the provider offers variants.
Supported Hls.js buffers, live fragment caches and HTTP relay URL tables are
bounded. Playwright drivers use a 512MiB Node old-space budget unless the user
supplied NODE_OPTIONS. This is not a hard limit on browser/GPU/native VLC memory.
Use the repository's monitor-resources.py to record a real host's 30-minute run.
